# The vendored tool trees are byte-for-byte copies of their upstream repositories:
# never apply end-of-line normalisation to them (-text).  Diffs stay enabled so a reviewer
# can still see textual changes.
evaluated_tools_and_configurations/tools/uEmu-test/** -text

# The overlays are byte-level artefacts too.  firmrca.patch carries CRLF pre-images for the two
# generated files in the checkout it patches; with core.autocrlf=input git rewrites them to LF on the
# way into the index, and the committed patch then no longer matches the file it patches — the overlay
# is rejected as a whole, mode entries included.  Never normalise a patch.
evaluated_tools_and_configurations/patches/*.patch -text

# The compiled ConvertFirmToELF helper is a static x86-64 binary; never let git touch its bytes.
evaluation_framework/framework/subprojects/akiba_modules/src/ConvertFirmToELF/resources/ELFBuilder/cmake-build-debug/ELFBuilder binary
